Creating with flags assigns self, sets priority and estimate, and prints the new issue's URL.
-- run --
linear issue create --title "Fix authentication bug" --description "Users are experiencing login issues" --assignee self --priority 2 --estimate 3 --team ENG --no-interactive
-- stdout --
✓ Created issue ENG-1: Fix authentication bug
https://linear.app/kadoraba/issue/ENG-1/fix-authentication-bug
-- stderr --
ENG-1 has no --project or --parent. Decide ownership from the candidate Project's full content and the related Initiative content (linear guide issue-authoring), then save the original read and set the project: (if [ -e original.json ] || [ -L original.json ]; then echo 'original.json exists' >&2; exit 1; fi; t=$(mktemp original.json.XXXXXX) || exit; s=0; linear issue view 'ENG-1' --json >| "$t" || { cat "$t" >&2; s=1; }; [ "$s" != 0 ] || ln "$t" original.json || s=1; rm -f "$t"; exit "$s") && linear issue update 'ENG-1' --project <project> --base-file original.json
-- mutations.json --
{"issueCreate": 1}
-- state.json --
{"Issue": [{"identifier": "ENG-1", "title": "Fix authentication bug", "description": "Users are experiencing login issues", "assignee": "0b000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "priority": 2, "estimate": 3}]}
